<article class="env-lemma" id="00G2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00G2">Lemma <span data-tag="00G2">10.35.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. If every prime ideal of $R$ is the intersection of the maximal ideals containing it, then $R$ is Jacobson. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediately clear from the fact that every radical ideal $I \subset R$ is the intersection of the primes containing it. See Lemma <a href="/tag/00E0" data-tag="00E0">10.17.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>